  "title": "NHS Surgeon Struck Off After Serious Surgical Error Left Patient Fighting for Life",
  "summary": "A former NHS consultant surgeon has been permanently removed from the medical register after a professional tribunal found that a serious surgical mistake during an emergency bowel operation placed a patient’s life at risk. The case, involving Dr Yasser Adly Abdel Rahman at Royal Oldham Hospital in Greater Manchester, raised concerns about surgical decision-making, patient safety, communication with families, and the importance of seeking assistance during complex medical procedures. According",
